{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"agent_message","text":"Profiling shows the projection is already near its practical optimum through rocBLAS; replacing it with a custom IEEE GEMM was both slower and numerically unsuitable. The promising change is structural: represent the fixed 2,432 features as 2,048 + 384 values inside a 2,048-lane reduction. That removes the 1,664 padded lanes while preserving the same paired reduction shape. I’m testing that before spending the second official attempt."}}
